# backups.conf.example
# Copy to ~/.config/sconl/backups.conf and customize.
# backupx reads ~/.config/sconl/backups.conf by default.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Format: name|method|source|dest|options
# {LOCAL_BASE}    → ~/_ on Linux, ~/Desktop/_ on Windows
# {RCLONE_REMOTE} → your rclone remote name (e.g. onedrive-sconl)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example:
# core|sync|{LOCAL_BASE}/core|{RCLONE_REMOTE}:_/core|--backup-dir {RCLONE_REMOTE}:_archivex/core
